{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:inflation:reconciler","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:e045892c9405fe63ab8cdf5577a5f62503a16e59fb5b2a3d4be3b8bfda66e33e","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"binary","positiveOutcomeId":"yes","probability":0.38},"questionHash":"sha256:a11e957a2fbf9e72130705a8815d67b5a6c66c3444a8332ee92cdcb4248068e1","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq2","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"WEIGHTING: Fermi Decomposer heaviest on the two-layer weight build and on the audit of the other panelists' arithmetic; Resolution Auditor heaviest on the EM-OECD floor and the one-way resolver latitude; Red-Team PARTIALLY ADOPTED on downward nominal rigidity (a real hit) and REJECTED on the drifted nominal anchor (a pose); Inside-View DOWN-WEIGHTED to near zero on conjunct A, because Fermi demonstrated his 0.30 is ~2.3x what his own mechanism implies (his path averages 2.135 and his weighted build 2.023; at the sd appropriate to a TEN-year average, ~0.35, that is P = 0.13, and recovering 0.30 needs sd ~0.6 pp on a decade average, which is implausible); Outside-View DOWN-WEIGHTED on conjunct A for the same reason Fermi caught — his own basket build gives 2.42 for the US-like case and his GDP-weighting line then enters the US at 2.7, an unexplained +0.29 pp upgrade that is the sole thing carrying his 0.52 over the line.\n\nCONJUNCT A (OECD-38 GDP-weighted core CPI/PCE avg >= 2.50%/yr, 2027-2036) = 0.58. Start from Fermi's two-layer build. Layer 1 (US-like core): shelter 0.33 @ 3.2 = 1.056; medical + social care services 0.09 @ 3.3 = 0.297; other labour-intensive core services 0.30 @ 2.7 = 0.810; core goods 0.23 @ 0.4 = 0.092; communication/digital 0.05 @ -0.8 = -0.040; plus electricity entering ONLY as second-round business cost (~2% energy share of service gross output x ~0.5 pass-through) +0.12 = 2.335. ACCOUNTING LOCK I KEEP FROM ALL THREE WAVE-1 PANELISTS: electricity is excluded from US core CPI/PCE and from HICP core by construction, so the 4-6% power/construction/care skew reaches the LEVEL only through that second-round channel; and consumer-facing AI-deflatables (telecom ~1.5-2%, media ~1%, education ~2.5%, household professional services <1%) are under 8% of core, so even a total J/K/M price collapse moves core by only -0.2 to -0.4 pp. Violent skew, modest level. TWO ADJUSTMENTS I MAKE. (i) RED-TEAM HIT ACCEPTED, DISCOUNTED BY HALF: core goods at 0.3-0.5% is a hyper-globalization number measured under maximum China supply, zero tariffs and no mineral constraint; under tariff/fragmentation/reshoring with downward nominal rigidity, sectors that \"want\" to deflate print 0 to +1.5%. I use 0.8%, not his 1.2% and not Wave 1's 0.4%: worth +0.09 on the US leg. (ii) Care services to 3.8% from 3.3% (+0.045), splitting the Inside-View's monopsony-rationing arrow against the Red-Team's median-voter arrow; the Red-Team's evidence that OECD medical and social-care CPI has outpaced core through austerity episodes is a genuine hit on the Inside-View's self-declared most load-bearing claim, but statutory settlements phase slowly and the fiscal squeeze (net interest 2% -> 3% of GDP) is real, so I move halfway. New US-like core 2.47. Layer 2 (2025 PPP GDP weights): re-running Fermi's vector with a uniform ~+0.12 uplift on the advanced legs and his EM legs unchanged takes the aggregate from 2.556 to ~2.65. THE SWING TERM IS STILL TURKEY AND IT IS ARITHMETIC: at a ~3.5% PPP weight Turkey alone contributes +0.27 pp; drop it and renormalize and the aggregate falls to ~2.38. Path check: 2027-2030 at ~2.95 and 2031-2036 at ~2.45 gives (4 x 2.95 + 6 x 2.45)/10 = 2.65, so the hurdle is cleared by the FRONT half plus the EM floor, not by 2030s stagflation. RESOLVER LATITUDE, MODELLED AS A MIXTURE RATHER THAN A HAIRCUT (the Auditor established it runs one way, down): 0.70 on a GDP-weighted CPI-style reading, central 2.65, sd 0.35 -> P = 0.67; 0.30 on a core-PCE-only or consumption-PPP-weighted reading (-0.25 pp on the US leg, lower EM contribution), central 2.42 -> P = 0.41. Blended P(A) = 0.70(0.67) + 0.30(0.41) = 0.59; take 0.58. RED-TEAM'S DRIFTED ANCHOR REJECTED AS A POSE: he infers a de facto ~3% target from the locked fiscal block, but names no transmission that moves a measured ten-year core average by 2036 — target revision is not a price index, inflation expectations in the locked priors are not unanchored, and his own reference class (high-debt aging democracies partially inflating debt) runs over 25-30 years, not nine. Granting him core goods but not the anchor is why I sit at 0.58 and not his 0.70.\n\nCONJUNCT B (China headline CPI < 1.50%/yr avg 2027-2036) = 0.68. Fermi's basket build is the most disciplined object in the effort: food 0.19 @ 1.5 + residence 0.21 @ 0.3 (rent-imputed, so a permanent -55/-60% property adjustment barely registers but delivers no rent growth) + other goods 0.25 @ -0.2 (capacity +5-7%/yr against domestic demand +3-4%/yr, PPI leakage) + services ex-residence 0.35 @ 1.6 = 0.858, taken to ~1.05 central for the 2026 basket rebase raising the services weight. Distance to threshold 0.45, sd 0.60 -> 0.77. I shade to 0.68 on the Red-Team's correctly identified ASYMMETRY of the no-tail, which Wave 1 under-weighted by leaning on a Japan 1995-2025 analogue that had no wage-floor policy, no hukou/rural-pension expansion and no pork cycle: a single +5% food year adds ~0.5 pp to a decade average, basket rebases in 2026 and 2031 shift weight toward services and lift prints, anti-involution capacity discipline is live policy, disorderly RMB depreciation imports food and energy, and NBS has a mild institutional reluctance to publish deflation. Against all that: a ~0.0-0.2% starting run rate, household income share stuck ~44% of GDP, and pension subsidies already ~10.1% of fiscal expenditure capping transfer-financed rebalancing. 0.68, below all three Wave-1 panelists (0.70-0.75) and above the Red-Team's 0.63.\n\nCORRELATION: mixed sign, netting slightly negative. The tradables channel is negative — Chinese goods deflation is itself the force holding my core-goods term at 0.8% rather than higher, so conditioning on A buys little extra on B — while the common OECD-physical-scarcity-versus-China-demand-deficit bifurcation is positive, and the tariff wall partly severs the negative channel (the Red-Team is right that this is the mechanism, which is exactly why my core-goods term moved). rho = -0.05 -> P(B|A) = 0.68 x 0.97 = 0.66. JOINT = 0.58 x 0.66 = 0.383 -> 38.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:52.789Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"Turkish annual CPI, as published by TurkStat, averages below 7.0% over calendar 2027-2029 (arithmetic mean of the three December-on-December prints), with Mexico, Chile and Colombia each averaging below 3.5% over the same three years.\",\"by_when\":\"Jan 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The cleanest single falsifier of MY numbers, because I have made this term the largest and most mechanical in the payload. It removes the ~+0.30 pp EM-OECD floor: my GDP-weighted OECD-38 core central falls from ~2.65 to ~2.45 and P(core >= 2.50 over 2027-2036) drops from 0.58 to ~0.38, taking CQ2 from 38 to ~26. The 2032-2036 central falls from 2.35 to ~2.18, cutting CQ6-C from 17 to ~11 and raising CQ6-D from 14 to ~20, with B roughly unchanged at ~57. CQ4 P50 falls ~15 bp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"US CPI core commodities (core goods) 12-month rate at or below 0.0% for calendar-year 2029, while Section 301/232-style tariff coverage remains in force at or above 2026 breadth.\",\"by_when\":\"Jan 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the one Red-Team hit I partially adopted — downward nominal rigidity converting the relative-price skew into the level. My core-goods term reverts from 0.8% to the Wave-1 plug of ~0.4% (-0.09 pp on the US leg, ~-0.07 pp on the aggregate), and with it the whole claim that tariffs and fragmentation have changed the regime in sectors that 'want' to deflate. CQ2 falls from 38 to ~32; CQ6-C from 17 to ~13 with the mass to B; CQ5 conjunct A falls ~0.03, taking CQ5 from 27 to ~25. It would also mean the Red-Team contrarian-posed on his single largest departure from Wave 1 and I should not have moved at all.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"China headline CPI (NBS monthly series, any basket vintage) prints 2.0% year-on-year or higher for four consecutive quarters at any point between 2027 and 2031, with the non-food, non-residence component contributing at least 1.0 pp of it (i.e. not a pork or energy spike).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Kills CQ2's stronger conjunct and the China-as-semi-independent-deflationary-object premise my effort brief required me to carry. P(China CPI < 1.50% over 2027-2036) falls from 0.68 to ~0.38 and CQ2 drops from 38 to ~22 even with my OECD leg fully intact — which is the cleanest available test of whether my CQ2 comes from the OECD leg (my claim) or from the correlation assumption. It also lifts my China real leg from 3.05% toward 3.4%, raising CQ3 P50 from 1.75 to ~1.88 and shifting ~4 points of CQ6 mass out of D into B and C.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Cumulative publicly disclosed AI-related capex impairments and cancellations stay below 10% of announced hyperscaler buildouts AND net external AI software/API revenue exceeds 1.0x annualized AI compute D&A for four consecutive quarters, with at least 70 GW of net firm capacity serving data centres reaching commercial operation across OECD-38 + China (EIA / ENTSO-E / CEC commissioning data) by end-2031.\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The highest-leverage signpost for my payload, because it removes the locked AI-Q4 bust from the middle of every 2032-2036 measurement window and simultaneously refutes my coupled claim that trades labour and interconnection bind harder than the dollars. Capital-services growth stays at ~1.8%/yr (+0.30 pp on the OECD leg) and the AI savings-demand term returns to +0.25 pp on r*. CQ3 P50 moves from 1.75 to ~2.05 and P90 from 2.75 to ~3.00; CQ4 P50 from 2.00 to ~2.30 with a thinner left tail; CQ6-A from 12 to ~19, D from 14 to ~9, B to ~57, C ~15; CQ5 falls from 27 to ~21 as the back-half MOVE path drops toward 85 and the leveraged-unwind shock source thins. It would also retire my AI-Q3 coupling correction.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"An equity drawdown of >= 20% (MSCI World, USD, closing basis) occurs in which the G7 GDP-weighted 10y nominal sovereign yield FALLS by >= 100 bp between the equity peak date and the trough date — the classic flight-to-quality reasserting itself despite convenience-yield erosion, basis-trade absorption and >100% debt/GDP.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the fiscal-dominance correlation structure behind both CQ5 and CQ4's right tail. P(no 50 bp rally | drawdown) falls from 0.45 to ~0.28 and the A|B conditional from 0.65 to ~0.52, taking CQ5 from 27 to ~16. CQ4 P90 falls from 3.35 to ~2.95 and the distribution loses its right skew. ~3 points of CQ6 mass move from C to D, because bond-market tolerance means repression is unnecessary and accommodation of inflation is less likely.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run1 wave 3 reconciler seat, effort 'inflation'."}}